Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Needle Unravels
- Story & Context: Deep inside Station 99, Elias found the transmitter melting into a puddle of lead as the first bolt hit the tower, causing the insulation to unravel like cheap thread. The smell of ozone was thick enough to taste, a sharp, bitter tang that coated his teeth. He clutched the controls, terrified that the storm was not weather, but a transmission. "The current knows my name before I speak it."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Macro photography of copper wire fraying into golden sparks against a backdrop of deep, bruised-purple storm clouds, hyper-realistic, high contrast.

Track 2: "Where are the fuses kept?"
- Story & Context: Mara hid in the basement of the ruined archives, her fingers tracing the rusted wall, asking the dark space the question that had haunted the station for years. She touched a patch of wet, cold concrete—the sensory imprint of a ghost—and realized the walls themselves were vibrating in time with the distant thunder. The conflict arose when she realized she was not the only one listening to the hum. "I am unmaking the room to see what breathes behind the plaster."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A cinematic, dimly lit shot of a trembling hand touching a cold, wet industrial concrete wall, silhouettes of abstract electrical arcs dancing in the background, moody and oppressive.

Track 3: Heddle’s Revenge
- Story & Context: Now the town of Heddle is a myth of scorched glass and silent antennas, where the looms are said to weave only the light of dead storms. A stranger found a shard of crystallized sand on the site, a fulgurite that pulsed with a faint, recorded rhythm. The aftermath remains a warning to all who try to map the erratic movements of the sky. "We mend the sky with needles of rain."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A conceptual image of a glass loom weaving threads of lightning into a fabric of dark, heavy iron, sharp focus, ethereal and dangerous, volumetric lighting.

